cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or data, please cite it as below."
title: "LLM gateway trust-boundary measurements: harness, synthetic data and results"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Elumalai
    given-names: Manikandan
    affiliation: "Independent Researcher"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0009-0049-6695"
version: "2026-11-09"
date-released: "2026-11-09"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Measurement harness, synthetic-data generators and results for an LLM gateway built on LiteLLM 1.102.1,
  acting as the trust boundary for agentic AI in regulated healthcare: added latency, failover under faults with a
  non-BAA fallback, tenant isolation, PHI detection, masking and restore (synthetic notes and the ASQ-PHI benchmark),
  load, scale-out across gateway worker counts, a 30-minute soak, a concurrent real-provider spot check, multi-turn
  agent runs with per-run budgets and key revocation, and stock LiteLLM 1.102.1 (with and without its own tag-based
  routing) under the same faults. Code under MIT; data and results under CC BY 4.0.
keywords:
  - LLM gateway
  - LiteLLM
  - PHI
  - de-identification
  - HIPAA
  - agentic AI
references:
  - type: dataset
    title: "ASQ-PHI"
    doi: "10.17632/csz5dzp7nx.1"
    notes: "Used as an external benchmark (E11); not redistributed here. Data in Brief, DOI 10.1016/j.dib.2026.112586."
    authors:
      - name: "The ASQ-PHI authors"
